;
; SPI master, Mode 0 only (CPOL=0, CPHA=0). SCK is side-set pin 0, MOSI
; is the OUT pin, MISO is the IN pin. CS is plain firmware-driven GPIO, not
; PIO — asserted before the SM starts clocking, released after the last RX
; byte is confirmed drained, no cycle-accurate CS/SCK relationship needed
; for the slave peripherals this is meant to talk to.
;
; Correctness is argued directly from what each instruction does, not from
; a memorized CPOL/CPHA truth table: MOSI is set up while SCK is held low
; ("side 0"), MISO is sampled while SCK is held high ("side 1") — data
; stable through the low phase, captured on the rising edge, is Mode 0 by
; definition. The [1] delay after each instruction gives a symmetric 50%
; duty cycle with margin either side of the sample point.
;
; Autopull/autopush must be enabled with an 8-bit threshold, shift left
; (MSB first) — configured in C, not here.
;
; Idle behavior: the loop always stalls (waiting for TX FIFO data via
; autopull) on the first instruction below, whose side-set value is 0 — so
; SCK sits low between transfers and between bytes, matching Mode 0's
; idle-low convention without any extra idle-state handling.
.program spi_master_mode0
.side_set 1

.wrap_target
    out pins, 1  side 0 [1]
    in  pins, 1  side 1 [1]
.wrap
